            <ArticleTitle>Allogeneic hematopoietic cell transplantation in an adult patient with Glanzmann thrombasthenia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1887-1890</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.1206</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Glanzmann thrombasthenia is a rare bleeding disorder that can present life-threatening bleeding. Our patients develop antiplatelet antibodies that become refractory to any pharmacological treatment. Allogeneic hematopoietic stem-cell transplantation is the only currently curative procedure, but has major risks mainly in adult; indeed, our patient died.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
